{"task_id": "Mbpp/165", "solution": "def count_char_position(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts characters in a string that match their position in the English alphabet (case insensitive).\n    For example, 'b' at index 1 or 'C' at index 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    ALPHABET = \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        if i < len(ALPHABET):\n            if char.lower() == ALPHABET[i]:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef find_even_pair(input_list: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs of integers in a list that xor to an even number.\n    A pair (a, b) XORs to an even number if a and b have the same parity.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs (num1, num2) where num1 comes before num2 in the list.\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            num1 = input_list[i]\n            num2 = input_list[j]\n\n            # The XOR result of two integers is even if and only if both integers have the same parity.\n            if (num1 % 2) == (num2 % 2):\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
