{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, etc.) to 1 in the given number.\n    Uses a 64-bit mask to perform the operation.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a mask with all even-positioned bits set to 1 (e.g., 0x55...).\n    # This 64-bit mask covers bit positions 0, 2, ..., 62.\n    even_bits_mask = 0x5555555555555555\n    \n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set the even bits.\n    return number | even_bits_mask"}
